nonland card revealed this way, add {G} and you gain 1 life. Then each player draws a card.', "Players can't gain life.\\nDamage can't be prevented.\\nAll damage is dealt as though its source had wither. (A source with wither deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)", 'Prismatic Geoscope enters the battlefield tapped.\\nDomain — {T}: Add X mana in any combination of colors, where X is the number of basic land types among lands you control.', "Psychosis Crawler's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.\\nWhenever you draw a card, each opponent loses 1 life.", "Put target artifact or creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. Shuffle Beacon of Unrest into its owner's library.", 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. It gains haste.\\nBasic landcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', "Rakdos Carnarium enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rakdos Carnarium enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {B}{R}.", "Realm Seekers enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the total number of cards in all players' hands.\\n{2}{G}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Realm Seekers: Search your library for a land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", "Redistribute any number of players' life totals. (Each of those players gets one life total back.)", "Return all artifact and enchantment cards from all graveyards to the battlefield under their owners' control. (Auras with nothing to enchant remain in graveyards.)", "Return all creatures blocking or blocked by target creature to their owner's hand.", "Return all creatures to their owners' hands.", "Return all nonland permanents to their owners' hands.\\nMiracle {1}{U} (You may cast this card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)", "Return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand. Volcanic Vision deals damage equal to that card's mana value to each creature your opponents control. Exile Volcanic Vision.", "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. Then that permanent's controller may sacrifice a land. If the player does, they may copy this spell and may choose a new target for that copy.", 'Reveal the top ten cards of your library. Starting with the next opponent in turn order, each opponent chooses a different nonland card from among them. Put the chosen cards into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'Reyhan, Last of the Abzan enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever a creature you control dies or is put into the command zone, if it had one or more +1/+1 counters on it, you may put that many +1/+1 counters on target creature.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)', 'Rootbound Crag enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Mountain or a Forest.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', "Rubblehulk's power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.\\nBloodrush — {1}{R}{G}, Discard Rubblehulk: Target attacking creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of lands you control.", 'Rugged Highlands enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rugged Highlands enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Rupture Spire enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rupture Spire enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you pay {1}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Sacrifice Dauntless Escort: Creatures you control gain indestructible until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice Sakura-Tribe Elder: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Sacrifice an artifact: Target artifact gains indestructible until end of turn.', 'Sandsteppe Citadel enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}, {B}, or {G}.', 'Savage Lands enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}, {R}, or {G}.', 'Search your library for a Plains, Island, Swamp, or Mountain card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nThreshold — If seven or more cards are in your graveyard, instead search your library for up to three basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the other into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Seaside Citadel enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}, {W}, or {U}.', "Selesnya Sanctuary enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Selesnya Sanctuary enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{W}.", "Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{U}.", 'Starting with you, each player separates all permanents they control into three piles. Then each player chooses one of their piles at random and sacrifices those permanents. (Piles can be empty.)', 'Strive — This spell costs {1}{G} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nChoose any number of target creatures. Double the number of +1/+1 counters on each of them.', 'Sunburst (This enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each color of mana spent to cast it.)\\n{1}, Remove four +1/+1 counters from Etched Oracle: Target player draws three cards.', 'Sunpetal Grove enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Forest or a Plains.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Suspend 4—{1}{R} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, pay {1}{R} and exile it with four time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.)\\nEach player discards their hand, then draws seven cards.', 'Swiftwater Cliffs enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Swiftwater Cliffs enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', "Target player sacrifices an attacking creature. You create X 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens, where X is that creature's toughness.", 'Tempting offer — Search your library for a land card and put it onto the battlefield. Each opponent may search their library for a land card and put it onto the battlefield. For each opponent who searches a library this way, search your library for a land card and put it onto the battlefield. Then each player who searched a library this way shuffles.', 'The owner of target nonland permanent shuffles it into their library, then draws two cards.', "The owner of target permanent shuffles it into their library, then reveals the top card of their library. If it's a permanent card, they put it onto the battlefield.", 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature on the battlefield.\\nBlasphemous Act deals 13 damage to each creature.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature your opponents control.\\nWhen Primeval Protector enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control.', 'Thornwood Falls enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Thornwood Falls enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Trample, indestructible\\nWhenever another creature you control attacks, it gains trample and indestructible until end of turn.', 'Trample\\nKalonian Hydra enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever Kalonian Hydra attacks, double the number of +1/+1 counters on each creature you control.', 'Trample\\nLieutenant — As long as you control your commander, Thunderfoot Baloth gets +2/+2 and other creatures you control get +2/+2 and have trample.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Tana, the Bloodsower deals combat damage to a player, create that many 1/1 green Saproling creature tokens.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)', 'Trample\\nWhenever Yidris, Maelstrom Wielder deals combat damage to a player, as you cast spells from your hand this turn, they gain cascade. (When you cast the spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.)', 'Trample\\nWhenever a player casts a spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Managorger Hydra.', "Trample\\nWilderness Elemental's power is equal to the number of nonbasic lands your opponents control.", 'Trample\\n{5}: Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.\\n{5}, Exile Soul of New Phyrexia from your graveyard: Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.', 'Transguild Promenade enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Transguild Promenade enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you pay {1}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Treacherous Terrain deals damage to each opponent equal to the number of lands that player controls.\\nBasic landcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nDestroy all creatures.', 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nDestroy two target creatures.', 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nExile two target creatures. For each of those creatures, its controller reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a creature card, puts that card onto the battlefield, then shuffles the rest into their library.', "Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nReturn all nonland permanents to their owners' hands.", 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nReturn up to two target cards from your graveyard to your hand. Exile Seeds of Renewal.', 'Untap all creatures you control and all creatures target opponent controls. You and that opponent each gain control of all creatures the other controls until end of turn. Those creatures gain haste until end of turn.', 'Untap all creatures. Until end of turn, whenever a creature an opponent controls blocks, draw a card.\\nDraw a card.', 'Vigilance, haste\\nAs Saskia the Unyielding enters the battlefield, choose a player.\\nWhenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, it deals that much damage to the chosen player.', 'When Breya, Etherium Shaper enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 blue Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.\\n{2}, Sacrifice two artifacts: Choose one —\\n• Breya deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n• Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.\\n• You gain 5 life.', "When Coiling Oracle enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a land card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put that card into your hand.", 'When Deepglow Skate enters the battlefield, double the number of each kind of counter on any number of target permanents.', 'When Elite Scaleguard enters the battlefield, bolster 2. (Choose a creature with the least toughness among creatures you control and put two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nWhenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it attacks, tap target creature defending player controls.', 'When Gamekeeper dies, you may exile it. If you do, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card. Put that card onto the battlefield and put all other cards revealed this way into your graveyard.', 'When Godo, Bandit Warlord enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Equipment card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\nWhenever Godo attacks for the first time each turn, untap it and all Samurai you control. After this phase, there is an additional combat phase.', 'When Ichor Wellspring enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Mycosynth Wellspring enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Myr Battlesphere enters the battlefield, create four 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature tokens.\\nWhenever Myr Battlesphere attacks, you may tap X untapped Myr you control. If you do, Myr Battlesphere gets +X/+0 until end of turn and deals X damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.", 'When Myr Retriever dies, return another target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Satyr Wayfinder enters the battlefield, reveal the top four cards of your library. You may put a land card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Trinket Mage enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an artifact card with mana value 1 or less, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Veteran Explorer dies, each player may search their library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "Whenever Armory Automaton enters the battlefield or attacks, you may attach any number of target Equipment to it. (Control of the Equipment doesn't change.)", 'Whenever Bruse Tarl, Boorish Herder enters the battlefield or attacks, target creature you control gains double strike and lifelink until end of turn.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)', 'Whenever Glint-Eye Nephilim deals combat damage to a player, draw that many cards.\\n{1}, Discard a card: Glint-Eye Nephilim gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever Wild Beastmaster attacks, each other creature you control gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is Wild Beastmaster's power.", "Whenever a creature an opponent controls attacks, if you're the defending player, create a 3/3 red Ogre creature token unless that creature's controller pays {3}.", 'Whenever a creature deals combat damage to one of your opponents, its controller may draw a card.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Whenever a creature you control attacks, defending player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\n{3}{R/W}{R/W}: Creatures your opponents control block this turn if able, and you choose how those creatures block.', 'Whenever a creature you control attacks, you may put a quest counter on Beastmaster Ascension.\\nAs long as Beastmaster Ascension has seven or more quest counters on it, creatures you control get +5/+5.', 'Whenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever a player casts a spell, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Forgotten Ancient.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may move any number of +1/+1 counters from Forgotten Ancient onto other creatures.', "Whenever an opponent casts a spell, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, you may put that card on the bottom of your library.", 'Whenever an opponent discards a creature card, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nWhenever an opponent discards a land card, add {B}{B}.\\nWhenever an opponent discards a noncreature, nonland card, draw a card.', 'Whenever an opponent plays a land, you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature and a +1/+1 counter on Juniper Order Ranger.', 'Whenever another creature with power 2 or less enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', 'Whenever one or more creatures attack, you may have target attacking creature gain double strike until end of turn.', "Whenever you cast your first spell each turn, choose an opponent at random. Vial Smasher the Fierce deals damage equal to that spell's mana value to that player or a planeswalker that player controls.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)", "Whenever you draw a card, put a +1/+1 counter on Chasm Skulker.\\nWhen Chasm Skulker dies, create X 1/1 blue Squid creature tokens with islandwalk, where X is the number of +1/+1 counters on Chasm Skulker. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Whenever you draw a card, you may put a hoofprint counter on Hoofprints of the Stag.\\n{2}{W}, Remove four hoofprint counters from Hoofprints of the Stag: Create a 4/4 white Elemental creature token with flying. Activate only during your turn.', 'Whipflare deals 2 damage to each nonartifact creature.', "Wight of Precinct Six gets +1/+1 for each creature card in your opponents' graveyards.", 'You have no maximum hand size.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you gain 1 life for each card in your hand.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'You may have Progenitor Mimic enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has "At the beginning of your upkeep, if this creature isn\'t a token, create a token that\'s a copy of this creature."', '[+2]: Discard up to two cards, then draw that many cards.\\n[−2]: Sacrifice an artifact. If you do, return target artifact card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n[−10]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an artifact is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield at the beginning of the next end step."\\nDaretti, Scrap Savant can be your commander.', '{1}, Sacrifice a nontoken artifact: Create a 1/1 blue Thopter artifact creature token with flying. You gain 1 life.', '{1}, {T}, Discard a card: You gain 4 life.\\n{1}, {T}, Pay 1 life: Create a 0/1 white Goat creature token.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Draw a card.', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', "{1}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Executioner's Capsule: Destroy target nonblack creature.", "{1}{B}{G}: Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains intimidate until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\n{2}{B}{G}, Sacrifice a nontoken creature: Create X 1/1 green Saproling creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's toughness.", "{1}{U}{R}: Return Etherium-Horn Sorcerer to its owner's hand.\\nCascade (When you cast this spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.)", '{1}{W}{U}, {T}: Return target artifact or enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{2}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{2}{B}, {T}, Exile Magus of the Will: Until end of turn, you may play lands and cast spells from your graveyard. If a card would be put into your graveyard from anywhere this turn, exile that card instead.', "{2}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Dispeller's Capsule: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.", '{3}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\n{3}{W}: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{4}: Scry 1, then reveal the top card of your library. If it's a land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped. Otherwise, draw a card.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)", "{5}, {T}: Target player mills X cards, where X is the number of cards in that player's graveyard.", '{G}: Exile target card from a graveyard. If it was a creature card, put a +1/+1 counter on Scavenging Ooze and you gain 1 life.', '{G}{U}, {T}: Double the number of each kind of counter on target artifact, creature, or land.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\nWhenever you tap Forbidden Orchard for mana, target opponent creates a 1/1 colorless Spirit creature token.', '{T}: Add two mana of any one color. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.', "{T}: Add {C} for each card you've drawn this turn.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)", '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity. If you spend this mana to cast your commander, it enters the battlefield with a number of additional +1/+1 counters on it equal to the number of times it's been cast from the command zone this game.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a storage counter on Dreadship Reef.\\n{1}, Remove X storage counters from Dreadship Reef: Add X mana in any combination of {U} and/or {B}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Buried Ruin: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Karplusan Forest deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Caves of Koilos deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Each player gains control of all creatures they own.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nWhenever you tap Zhur-Taa Druid for mana, it deals 1 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {U}.', "{T}: Choose any number of target creatures. Each of those creatures gains persist until end of turn. (When it dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", '{T}: Draw two cards. Target opponent gains control of Humble Defector. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Each player draws a card.', '{T}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, destroy all nonland permanents.', '{U}: Target noncreature artifact becomes an artifact creature with power and toughness each equal to its mana value until end of turn.\\n{W}{B}: Target artifact creature gains deathtouch and lifelink until end of turn.', "{W}{U}, {T}: Put a bribery counter on target creature you don't control. Its controller draws a card.\\nCreatures with bribery counters on them can't attack or block."]
flavor: ['"A crafter must imbue her weapon with part of her soul—something the Phyrexians are incapable of doing."\\n—Melira, sylvok outcast', '"A richer people could give more but they could never give as much."', '"As long as my hand holds a blade, there\'s hope for a pure Mirrodin once again."', '"By the time your knees have worn through your robe, you may have begun to learn your place."', '"Dance, and bring forth the coil! It is an umbilical to Gaea herself, fattening us with the earth\'s rich bounty."', '"Do not try to make sense of the chimera. Impossibility is its habitat."\\n—Kydele, prophet of Kruphix', '"Don\'t be so quick to reclaim the thawing lands. They might have acquired a taste for freedom."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"Etherium is limited. Innovation is not."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Even your blade knows who will triumph here."\\n—Atraxa, Praetors\' Voice', '"Everyone has a price."', '"From shards and splinters I call forth my living horde."\\n—Molimo, maro-sorcerer', '"Fuses? We have more than enough! Now . . . which one was it?"\\n—Flearan One-Eye, goblin engineer', '"Greed, rage, and bloodlust all lead to death at the hands of those who keep their heads."\\n—Sergeant Eyra', '"Greet death with sword in hand."', '"Her voice is justice, clear and relentless."\\n—Akroma, angelic avenger', '"Holy places are no longer sanctuary from death, and death is no longer sanctuary from anything."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"How does one become a self-taught genius? Naturally, it requires brains."', '"How truly vast this city must be, that I have traveled so far and seen so much, yet never once found the place where the buildings fail."', '"I am not at liberty to reveal my sources, but I can assure you, the price on your head is high."', '"I came seeking a challenge. All I found was you."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"I craved enlightenment, and Crucius\'s etherium opened my eyes. I would share my sight with you, but first you must believe."', '"I find its symmetry pleasing. It rids our world of offensive refuse while disposing of itself."\\n—Dolomarus, Proctor of the Clean', '"I never thought I\'d spend my life fighting. I\'m a maker, not a destroyer."', '"I used to hurl rocks and eat scraps of meat burned over a fire. Look at what I\'ve become and tell me Simic does not hold infinite possibility."', '"I used to joke that he had been exiled for being too smart. Now I know why he never laughed."\\n—Glissa Sunseeker', '"I\'ve seen death before. My mother succumbing to illness, my comrades bleeding on the battlefield . . . But I\'d never seen anything as dreadful as that."\\n—Taani, berserker of Etlan', '"If that brain can\'t figure out the secret of the serum, then add more brains."\\n—Rhmir, Hand of the Augur', '"In these halls there is no pass or fail. Your true test comes with the first full moon."', '"Infiltrate and infuriate!"\\n—Goblin Espionage League motto', '"It lives . . . IT LIVES!"\\n—Ludevic, necro-alchemist', '"It reflects the purity of Mirrodin-that-was."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"Let your heels point you home."\\n—Ancient blessing', '"Life can be found in all things, even things unnatural."\\n—Multani, maro-sorcerer', '"Look what we fought for. Look what we built together."', '"May the memory of our fallen heroes ensnare the violent hearts of lesser men."\\n—Great Threshold of Monserkat inscription', '"Monsters dwell in every heart. We only think civilization tames them." ―Euphemia, Nexus watcher', '"Naga shed their scales. We wear ours with pride."\\n—Golran, dragonscale captain', '"Nature is a wonderful engineer but works far too slowly for my tastes."', '"Now the scaled ones rule Tarkir."', '"Once I supply the breeze, you\'ll see your warriors for the smoke they truly are."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"Only a mind unfettered with the concerns of the flesh can see the world as it truly is."', '"Only the decadent think magic should be pristine and without cost."', '"Only the weak imprison themselves behind walls. We live free under the wind, and our freedom makes us strong."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"Our glorious infection has taken hold."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"The Lowlands refuse to suffer at the whims of the High City."', '"The cost of your opposition will be extracted from your wits."\\n—Nekusar, the Mindrazer', '"The land grows only where the kami will it."\\n—Dosan the Falling Leaf', '"The light of my master\'s guidance traverses all boundaries, even those separating life and death."', '"The most enlightened mages create beauty from violence."\\n—Medomai the Ageless', '"The most powerful dreams visit those who shelter in a dragon\'s skull."\\n—Chianul, Who Whispers Twice', '"The world is a puzzle, and the mind is its key."', '"There is great wisdom in rushing headlong into combat . . . if you\'re prepared."\\n—Kenjek, captain of the Thousand Swords', '"These eyes have shown me the flaws of flesh."', '"They say the ruins of Sedraxis were once a shining capital in Vithia. Now it is a blight, a place to be avoided by the living."\\n—Olcot, Rider of Joffik', '"Those may be the squirms of one life ending or of another beginning. Either way, I\'d leave it alone."\\n—Rakka Mar', '"Those who are different are untrustworthy, unpredictable. Put your safety in the hands of your own kind."\\n—Bowen, Barrenton guardcaptain', '"Through me, the Great Teacher\'s voice will rattle this world."', '"Through the haze of battle I saw the glint of sun on golden mane, the sheen of glory clad in mail, and I dropped my sword and wept at the idiocy of war."\\n—Dravin, Gruul deserter', '"To spend your life seeking, only to find regret upon achieving . . . this is the most delicious irony of all."\\n—Leshrac, Walker of Night', '"We are all decaying, always in a state of near-death. One moment without breath and we begin to break down."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"We give the audience what they want."\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"We must rely on our own knowledge, not on the dogma of the seekers or the mutterings of the sphinxes."\\n—Tullus of Palandius', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"When gods become apathetic, the people will worship anyone who answers their pleas."\\n—Kiora', '"When something dies, all things benefit. Well okay, just our things."\\n—Ezoc, Golgari rot farmer', '"When they covered the world in city, all they did was give themselves nowhere to run."', '"You are beneath contempt. Your lineage will be forgotten."', '"You were once Mardu, so your body and will are strong. Now we must train your mind."\\n—Houn, Jeskai elder', '"You\'ll bend to my will—with or without your precious sanity."', "A Planeswalker's chronicle spans worlds and civilizations, each page a lifetime.", "A body clad in steel reflects a warrior's resolve.", "A savage hunter with a prince's bearing.", "A single festercreep isn't alone. It's already an infestation.", 'After lightning struck the cliffs, the ore became iron, the iron became steel, and the steel became greaves. The lightning never left.', "Alara's burning blood cannot be contained by mere earth and stone.", 'All are prey to the eyes of the wild.', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'An eye for detail, a mind for numbers, a soul of clockwork.', 'An overwhelming sense of calm accompanies the gryffs that wheel above the roofs of Gavony.', 'Anarchy comes in many forms: social, individual, Gruul . . .', "Any creature on a druid's shoulder is his family, any land under his feet his home.", 'Art is unknown to the vedalken—for them, all creations must serve a purpose.', 'As it spins, dead voices shriek in an ever-increasing cacophony, rending the mind asunder.', 'As long as one drop of the oil exists, the joyous work continues.', 'As their supplies of etherium dwindled, mechanists sent gargoyles farther and farther afield in search of salvage.', "Avacyn's holy warriors kept hope alive in her darkest hours. Now they will carry that hope across Innistrad.", 'Beneath crashing waves lies an ocean of secrets waiting to be explored.', 'Beyond pain, beyond obsession and wild despair, there lies a place of twisted power only the most tormented souls can reach.', 'Countless delights drift on the surface while dark schemes run below.', 'Depending on your point of view, the seal represents a proud guardian of the natural cycle or one who has sold her soul to darkness for eternal life.', 'Dimir mages put the lanterns to good use, creating shapeshifters and sleeper agents from mana foreign to them.', 'Do not fear the lightning. Fear the one it obeys.', 'Each flower identical, every leaf and petal disturbingly exact.', "Elspeth's squires do not seek advancement. For them, no knightly glory could surpass the glory of serving their champion.", 'Enduring the most desolate and dangerous conditions, Abzan sentries unfailingly guard the stronghold gates.', "Enlightenment is not gained by striking the bell or hearing its toll. It's found in the silence that follows.", 'Esper mages devised their weapons to be so devastating that war seemed unnecessary.', 'Even baloths fear its feeding time.', 'Even the lost and undead need a protector.', 'Exhale, and let the winds carry your soul for all eternity.', 'Fight with a friend at your back, steel in your hands, and magic in your veins.\\n—Quirion creed', 'First, whispers of ancient days. Then, visions of things to come.', 'For the Simic Combine, its sigil serves not as an emblem of honor but as a trademark. Its familiar image on any biological commodity attests to superb craftsmanship, ingenious innovation, and higher cost.', "For wisdom's sake, it was built high to gaze on all things. For glory's sake, it was built high as a testament of power. For strength's sake, it was built high to repel all attacks.", 'Forever after, she lived in fear of the madness reclaiming her.', 'Goblins generally have two possessions: one per hand.', 'Gruul territorial markings need not be legible. The blood, snot, and muck used to smear them are unmistakably Gruul.', 'Her bold movements are anchored in the careful precision of each rope.', 'History has buried its treasures deep.', "If you hear it, it's too late.", 'In a wave of spells called the Cursemute, Avacyn cleansed the world with divine fire.', 'In nature, not a single bone or scrap of flesh goes to waste.', 'Inscribed with runes that predate the dragon, its horns possess their own ancient magic.', 'It evades Phyrexians by hiding in the spaces between seconds.', 'It harmonizes with the essence of its master.', "It's hard to argue with a force made of divine will.", 'Its beak rends flesh and bone, exposing the tender marrow of dream.', 'Its blood is life. Its body is growth.', 'Its flight sets the sky itself on fire.', 'Its graceful glide paints the ocean floor with strokes of luminescence.', 'Jund is a world as cruel as those who call it home. Their brutal struggles scar the land even as it carves them in its image, a vicious circle spiraling out of control.', 'Life is such a fragile thing.', "Lost to time is the artificer's art of trapping light from a distant star in a ring of purest gold.", 'Lumengrid, site of the Knowledge Pool, source of vedalken arcana.', 'Made of bone and boiled in blood, a Rakdos signet is not considered finished until it has been used as a murder weapon.', "Many who cross Sorin's path come down with a sudden and fatal case of being-in-the-way-of-a-millennia-old-vampire.", 'Mephidross gives up treasure easily . . . as long as you take its place.', 'Murky Otarian tides hide the forgotten treacheries of the Phyrexian war.', 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', 'On Naya, ambition and treachery are scarce, hunted nearly to extinction by the awe owed to terrestrial gods.', 'On Otaria, peace and harmony are rare. Places that provide both are cherished.', 'Once guarded by the Knights of the Reliquary, the tower stands now protected only by its own remoteness, its dusty treasures open to plunder by anyone.', 'One quiet word sets off the stampede.', "Only the sun that beats down upon Arashin's walls could shine more brightly.", 'She bears the greatest burden of all: that of knowing.', 'Snaking remnants of nature directed by a body of thought and progress, the oracles embody all that is Simic.', 'Some see the world as a place of infinite wonder and knowledge. Some see it as an infinite dinner plate.', 'Something roams the killing places, sniffing the guilt of the slayers, stalking them on iron paws.', 'Sometimes death comes knocking. Sometimes it tears down the walls.', 'Spitting is the customary greeting between a creature and its magical impostor.', 'Structures built from darksteel yield to neither assault nor age.', 'Such cloaks are in high demand both by assassins and by those who fear them.', 'Survival is a constant competition from which both sides can benefit.', 'Take two steps north into the unsettled future, south into the unquiet past, east into the present day, or west into the great unknown.', 'That which endures, survives.', 'Thaumaturges remain silent around chimeras, lest their words conjure even stranger beasts.', 'The Abzan turn to this spell only as a last resort, for its inevitable result is what they most dread: to be alone.', 'The Orzhov care not for repentance, only repayment.', 'The Rakdos believe that all are eager to join their revels, even when told otherwise.', 'The best techniques outlive their creators.', 'The carnage of conflicts long past still stains the Otarian soil.', 'The dense jungle surrenders to a lush and lavish expanse. At its center uncoil the spires of Qarsi Palace.', 'The earth shook in support of their cause, offering a champion of its own.', 'The fastest way across the dunes is above.', 'The first satyr to wake after a revel must search for the site of the next one.', 'The first vine shows the others where to grow.', "The form of the sigil is just as important as the sigil itself. If it's carried on a medallion, its bearer is a master. If it's tattooed on the body, its bearer is a slave.", 'The greatest masters of the craft abandon tools altogether, shaping metal with hand and mind alone.', 'The mind is a beautiful bounty encased in an annoying bone container.', "The mine's riches never end, nor do the moans of the spirits doomed to haunt them.", 'The oil created the mycosynth. The mycosynth created New Phyrexia.', "The pounding of his followers' hearts matched the beat of his hooves, and their voices echoed his bellows.", 'The power of a waterfall. The fury of an avalanche. The intellect of a gale-force wind.', "The sea filled the villagers' nets until the day it cast its own.", 'The slag-workers wasted no time in creating their own flare pulses to cleanse the area of the *incompleat*.', 'The smallest seed of regret can bloom into redemption.', 'The stature of the fighter matters less than the depth of the cut.', 'The vedalken embed such urns in their living artifact creations.', 'There is always a moment of trepidation before opening a message capsule, for fear of the judgment that might be contained within.', 'There were no tombstones in orochi territory. Slain warriors were buried with a tree sapling, so they would become a part of the forest after death.', 'To gain audience with the hegemon, one must bring a riddle she has not heard.', 'To protect the alliance between Kjeldor and Yavimaya, they trained in the ways of both.', "Unaware of Lorwyn's diversity, it sees only itself, reflected a thousand times over.", "Warning to those who scale the cliffs without paying tribute: It's a long way down.", 'We shall suffer turmoil equal to that which we have wrought, whether in this life or the next.', 'Weakness is not in the nature of the Swarm.', 'When asked how many paths reach enlightenment, the monk kicked a heap of sand. "Count," he smiled, "and then find more grains."', 'When defeat is near and guidance is scarce, all eyes look in one direction.', 'When it awoke, it shook the plane with the thunder of its craving.', 'When night fell, the plane itself was scarred.', 'When the vaults are empty, everyone is rich.', "With no flesh to tire or resolve to falter, the machines soon became the Academy's preferred trainers.", 'Without the interfering hands of civilization, nature will always shape itself to its own needs.', 'Worse than the years of aging was the burden of memory. The young monk lost his youth and gained a vicarious lifetime of hardship and woe.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony Jones', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Austin Hsu', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Despain', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Charles Urbach', 'Chase Stone', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Kendall', 'David A. Cherry', 'David Gaillet', 'David Martin', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Doug Chaffee', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'James Zapata', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Kang', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'Jon Foster', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josh Hass', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Jung Park', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Sass', 'Monte Michael Moore', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Omar Rayyan', 'Paolo Parente', 'Paul Bonner', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Whitters', 'Richard Wright', 'Ron Brown', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott Hampton', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Shelly Wan', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stephan Martiniere', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tommy Arnold', 'Tony Foti', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'William Wu', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'YW Tang', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
